  "steps": [
    "Add butter to a pan then add walnuts. Toast it then add apple. Cook for 3-4 minutes until apples become soft. Add cinnamon, salt, sweetener and water.",
    "Add the cornstarch slurry and cook until the filling becomes thick and jammy. There should be no watery syrup.",
    "Let the apple filling cool completely before rolling.",
    "Mix the milk, cornstarch, oil and cinnamon to dip rice papers.",
    "Dip each rice paper sheet for only about 2 seconds and stack 2 sheets together for each roll.",
    "Add the apple filling and roll tightly like a burrito.",
    "Lightly brush the rolls with oil.",
    "Air fry at 190°C for 12 to 16 minutes, flipping around 8 minutes.",
    "For extra crunch, air fry at 200°C for another 2 to 3 minutes. Remove only when completely crunchy and serve with sweet yogurt dip! The cold and hot combo is insane."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The creator gives about 120–130 kcal and 3 g fibre per roll; we use the upper figure.",
    "The optional yogurt dressing adds 200 kcal and 25 g protein."
  ],
